===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
Oracle bone inscriptions often wrote {{lang|zh|后}} as {{och-l|*毓}}, depicting a woman giving birth. Wang Guowei posits the meaning extended from childbirth to succession, then to empress. In the modern form, the birthing figure would be {{och-l|*𠂆}} and the child figure {{och-l|*𠮛}}.<ref name="說文新證">季旭昇，2004《說文新證》，台北：藝文印書館印行，2014年9月第二版。p.708-709</ref>

According to ''Kōjien''<ref group="zh">{{R:Kojien}}</ref> and 学研漢和大字典, {{Han compound|nocap=1|ls=ic|人|口|t1=person (variant form)|t2=hole}} — a depiction of a person's ({{m|zh|人|tr=-}}) anus, with the additional meaning of “behind”, “rear”, as well as coming to mean “emperor/empress”, who would live in a palace “behind” worldly troubles.

