===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|いのち}}
From {{inh|ja|ojp|-|sort=いのち}}, from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*inəti|sort=いのち}}. Probably a compound of Old Japanese elements {{compound|ja|sort=いのち|息|tr1=i|t1=breath|pos1=''i'' in compounds, ''iki'' on its own|の|tr2=no|pos2=possessive particle|霊|tr3=chi|t3=spirit, force, soul}}.<ref>{{R:ja:SMKGGJT|p=91}}</ref>

Some analyses describe this as a compound using {{m|ja|生|tr=i||life, breath|pos=''i'' in compounds, ''iki'' on its own}} as the initial semantic element. This is equally valid, as {{m|ja|息|tr=iki}} and {{m|ja|生き|tr=iki}} are cognates.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|いのち|acc=1|acc_ref=DJR}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|いのち}}

# [[life]]
#: {{ja-usex|'''命'''の[[恩%人]]|'''いのち''' の おん%じん|person to whom one owes their '''life'''}}
# [[lifespan]]
# [[lifetime]]
# [[fate]], [[destiny]]
# {{lb|ja|sort=いのち|figuratively}} the most [[important]] part or [[aspect]] of a thing

=====Usage notes=====
{{lang|ja|命}} as "life" is distinct from several other Japanese words that may also be translated to English as "life". In particular, it means "the state of being alive, an animating force, or life as a whole (from birth to death)". Compare the terms below, which may also be rendered as "life" in English:
* {{m|ja|生活|tr=seikatsu|t=life}}: Day-to-day life as it is experienced; lifestyle; one's usual activities, habits, and routines.
* {{m|ja|生存|tr=seizon|t=life}}: Action involved in staying alive, as in "signs of life".
* {{m|ja|生命|tr=seimei|t=life}}: Biological life in general, particularly in scientific contexts.
* {{m|ja|存在|tr=sonzai|t=life}}: Being; either the state of existing or a thing that exists.
* {{m|ja|人生|tr=jinsei|t=life}}: A person's narrative, experience, and/or accomplishments from birth to death.
* {{m|ja|寿命|tr=jumyō|t=life}}: Lifespan or life expectancy.
* {{m|ja|残機|tr=zanki|t=life}}: A video-game life; a chance to play.
* {{m|ja|元気|tr=genki|t=life}}: Liveliness.

